; TEST: abort=1
;
; `chk %i %n` traps when %i >= %n (ssa-ir.md 2.3), compared UNSIGNED (`jae`).
; The lowering's `a[i]` shape (lowering.md's `Index` row) at i = N = 4, one
; past a four-element u32 array: the trap must come before the `index` and
; the `load` it guards, which would read past the array. Kind 1, "failed
; `chk`" (prelude/README.md). memory_narrow.ir passes `chk` at i = 2 and 3.
;
; Mutation (run): `jae` as `ja` (so i = N passes) -> exit 7.

functio @initium (ptr) -> u8 {
b0:
%0 = param ptr 0
%1 = slot 16 4
%2 = iconst u64 4
%3 = iconst u64 4
chk %3 %2
%4 = index %1 %3 4
%5 = load u32 %4 0 nativus
%6 = iconst u8 7
ret %6
}
